  "limitations": [
    "Memory measures bare parameter reads including parameter integrity checks; it does not include live source-owner enrollment, revocation, Objective/NDU or complete native service handling.",
    "Two warmups plus 18 measured calls per arm; three exposed question forms repeated six times are not 18 independent tasks.",
    "The source comparator is exact typed retrieval over two verified source observations, not a general strong RAG/repair agent.",
    "This is one short sequential warm probe; p95 is the maximum at N18. No sustained scale, tail SLA or hardware-general superiority claim.",
    "Startup inside the worker excludes earlier interpreter/main-module setup; whole child includes it. Source startup CPU recorded 0 reflects counter granularity, not free execution.",
    "Shared controller CPU covers both arms and complete pre/post hash checks, including audit retention. It is not imputed equally to arms or erased from the study total.",
    "Outer waited-process CPU covers controller+children and CLI/receipt overhead. The small residual is not measured again; never add overlapping totals.",
    "Source bytes are logical observation-payload reads, not physical I/O. Memory source-bytes 0 does not mean zero base/checkpoint/runtime reads.",
    "Peak RSS is the direct-child high-water observation, not whole-host peak; library/OS/page-cache sharing remains outside that number.",
    "Process IDs are invocation-namespace identifiers; no globally unique process or remote attestation claim.",
    "Whole-host CPU, external launcher self CPU, energy, billing, dynamic-library closure and continuous/transient storage remain unknown.",
    "No protocol change or retry occurred after outcomes. Source, checkpoint and runtime pins were checked before first query and after both arms by the frozen controller.",
    "The source and model runtime snapshots are retained dependencies, including later relay packages; whole OS and minimum install closure remain unknown.",
    "Group independence and cost-closure flags in the reusable quality reducer are controller declarations; they require future linkage to a frozen incident catalogue and execution receipts.",
    "Fixed source-first order, one local runtime and a tiny repeated sample; these observations cannot establish broad quality, scale, causal hardware superiority or independent future transfer."
  ],
